    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0743" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862S.01/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Whitlock</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-07T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>39. Herrick has been instructed to repeat to you Department’s memorandum on A and
                    B mandates.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d369-f1"/> On receipt of his telegram please
                    transmit immediately to Foreign Office for its information text of
                    memorandum.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d369-f1" n="2" xml:id="d369-f1-content">
                <p>For text of memorandum, see telegram no. 377, Aug. 7, 1921, to the Ambassador in
                    France, <ref target="frus1921v01#pg_922"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>,
                        vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 922</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
